course: dictionary
lesson: 3761
title: One word, two jobs: foal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A foal is a baby horse, donkey or zebra. «A foal must walk soon so it can keep up with the herd and run from danger.» The herd is the group of animals the foal travels with, so a foal is a young animal that must learn to move fast.
explain: Foal can also be a verb, which is a doing word. When a mare foals, she gives birth to a foal. In «The mare foaled early in the morning», foaled is what the mare did, not a thing. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or an action?
explain: Clues in the sentence help you choose. Words like «a», «the» or «her» before foal usually show it is a noun, a thing. Words like «will» or «did» before it usually show it is a verb, an action.
fact: Foal means a baby horse, donkey or zebra.
fact: «A newborn foal» means a foal that has only just been born.
fact: «The mare and her foal» means the mother horse and her baby.
fact: «In foal» means pregnant, so a mare in foal is going to have a baby.
fact: Some babies, like foals and baby giraffes, can walk within hours of birth, while kittens, puppies and human babies are born helpless and need long care.
exercise: «A foal must walk soon so it can keep up with the herd.» What is a foal? | A field where animals run | A grown-up mare that has a baby | A group of animals that walk together | *A baby horse, donkey or zebra
exercise: «The mare foaled early in the morning.» In this sentence, what does foaled mean? | Stood very still in a field | Ran away from the herd | *Gave birth to a foal | Grew very tall
exercise: What does the phrase «in foal» mean? | Happy after a long walk | *Pregnant, so a baby is on the way | Hungry for fresh grass | Lost in a field
test: In «In 2020 a Przewalski's horse foal called Kurt was cloned», what kind of animal was Kurt? | *A horse | Giraffe | Zebra | Donkey
test: In the sentence «The mare will foal next week», is foal a noun or a verb? | Adjective | *Verb | Noun
exam: Which sentence uses foal as a noun, a thing? | «The herd ran across the field» | *«The foal stood up on its wobbly legs» | «She foaled twice last year» | «The mare will foal in May»
